<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sogdians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sogdian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sogdians were an Iranian people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>, famed as merchants along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. They served as traders, diplomats and administrators for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>. The Tang Dynasty profile notes their commercial and military roles, including in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a>.</p></div>
